# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte; EMUSEN_DIANASH_GOLDEN=record rewrites it - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command cpus
usage 1   cpus                          list the processors a debug command can be scoped to

case the fake target's processors
target fake
covers 1
$ cpus
out 317
GOLDEN debug processors:
  cpu   PC=$008003  the main processor
        supports: bp, cov, bt, regs, setreg, disasm   code space: CpuBus
  gsu   PC=$000020  a graphics coprocessor
        supports: cov, regs, disasm   code space: VRAM
Scope a command by putting the name first, e.g. `bp sa1 add 8000` or `cov gsu on`.
status 0
action none
$ cpus extra
out 317
GOLDEN debug processors:
  cpu   PC=$008003  the main processor
        supports: bp, cov, bt, regs, setreg, disasm   code space: CpuBus
  gsu   PC=$000020  a graphics coprocessor
        supports: cov, regs, disasm   code space: VRAM
Scope a command by putting the name first, e.g. `bp sa1 add 8000` or `cov gsu on`.
status 0
action none
end

case a bare target
target bare
covers 1
$ cpus
out 75
GOLDEN publishes no per-CPU debug list; every command targets its main CPU.
status 0
action none
end

case with no target
target none
covers 1
$ cpus
out 65
Error: No ROM loaded - this command needs an active debug target.
status 1
action none
$ echo $?
out 1
1
status 0
action none
end

case on venus
target venus
covers 1
$ cpus
out 337
SNES debug processors:
  cpu   PC=$00ED3E  Ricoh 5A22 (65816) main CPU
        supports: bp, cov, bt, regs, setreg, disasm   code space: CpuBus
  spc   PC=$00FFCF  Sony SPC700 sound CPU
        supports: bp, cov, regs, setreg, disasm   code space: APURAM
Scope a command by putting the name first, e.g. `bp sa1 add 8000` or `cov gsu on`.
status 0
action none
end

